{
  "notes": "T8 plan: Hatti spent T6-T7 conquering Ugarit (fleet) and Carchemish (kanesh army), kizzuwatna army giving the supports. Kanesh army, probably my T5 unseen supporter, is now away at carchemish, so Tuwanuwa defence is likely 2 (tuwanuwa + kizzuwatna) or 3 if hattusa holds an army. Try the strike again: seha->tuwanuwa, mira and lukka support (3), fleet westsea supports lukka hold. A bounce costs nothing (T5 precedent). A win destroys the Hatti army and gains Tuwanuwa 30. Lukka is safe: only kizzuwatna and tuwanuwa armies touch it (max 2 vs my hold 2, ties bounce); Hatti fleet is at ugarit, needs a turn to reach cilicia. Treasury 20, income 125 = upkeep 125. c11, c12 due home about T9: back pay about 88, I can pay only about 20; they will likely give notice, renew only if cheap. Wake T9 to read the result. If Tuwanuwa is mine: seha army stays there, mira and lukka support its hold. If it bounced: decide whether to repeat or sit. Free city-states are all taken; only conquest from Hatti can grow me. Consider disbanding the fleet (35 a season) only if Hatti fleet stays far from Lukka.",
