{
  "notes": "T8: Egypt took Byblos T7 (A gaza->byblos by sea, F syriansea supporting). Byblos is gone, so my scheduled T13 buy is cancelled (empty entry). All free cities near me are now taken (Ugarit Hatti, Qadesh Babylonia, Byblos Egypt): no purchase is left, income stays 20 (Amurru only). GRAVE DANGER: Egypt army in Byblos plus Egypt fleet in syriansea can both reach Amurru: army byblos->amurru supported by the fleet is strength 2 against walls 1 and takes it; then I have no land and fall. I cannot garrison walls and have no units or envoys, so I cannot stop it this season. Only help: a friendly king supports Amurru's walls holding (Hatti F ugarit is adjacent to amurru) or Egypt agrees to leave it. I rehired c13 (26) and c14 (14), term 8, at the end of T8; they can be sent from T9. I wake in T9. PLAN T9: c14 to Egypt: nonaggression tablet (Egypt sends no troops or ships against Amurru; I send none against Egypt's holdings), brother greeting, up to about 50 gold as a gift only if Egypt seals; show k5 k11 k19 so Egypt sees friends watching Amurru. c13 to Hatti: ask F ugarit to support Amurru's walls holding each season Egypt is near; share Egypt fleet news (syriansea beside Amurru and Ugarit); propose Hatti, Arzawa, and one more strike Cyprus: taker may keep Tamassos if it cedes Enkomi to me. If gold allows, a third envoy to Arzawa with the same. Keep wages low: dismiss envoys once they are back and idle. Do not waste gold: strength is gold plus 10 x yield.",
  "summary": "Alashiya, smallest kingdom (start 1200). T1 bought Amurru (walls, yield 20, cannot garrison). T2 k5 with Arzawa (no ships or troops against each other, warn of harm). T2 k11 and T4 k19 with Hatti (peace; Ugarit in Hatti's reach; Hatti sends nothing against Enkomi/Tamassos; word before quarrel). Egypt fleets took Tamassos (T3) and Enkomi (T4): my fleet and capital lost. I hold only Amurru, no units, cannot levy until I hold a home province again (levy needs an empty home province). T5 asked Hatti and Arzawa to strike Egypt's fleets in Cyprus (150 per province on receipt): T7 answers: both refuse to seal or send ships for now; both want word of Egypt's fleets; Arzawa strikes only if Egypt's ships come at its coast or Hatti and another truly join. Hatti took Ugarit T6. Egypt took Byblos T7 and now has an army in Byblos and a fleet in syriansea next to Amurru: Amurru is in danger (if it falls my kingdom falls). No free city is left to buy. T7 I dismissed c13 and c14 to save gold; T8 rehired both (26 and 14, term 8) to send from T9. Standings T8: Egypt 2.08, Babylonia 1.64, Hatti 1.42, Arzawa 1.25, Mitanni 1.21, Assyria 0.81, me 0.24. Only way up: allies break Egypt's two fleets in Cyprus (needs 3 fleets: one attacks Enkomi to cut support, one attacks Tamassos with the third supporting) and cede a province to me; then I raise a unit there. Income 20, treasury 209 at T8.",
  "ledger": [
