  "notes": "T8 plan. Treasury 410 at orders, nothing spent. Orders: A_byblos -> amurru, F_syriansea supports (2 v walls 1); A_gaza -> byblos convoyed by F_levantsea. This ends Alashiya (no land). Delta army D stays home, enkomi/tamassos fleets hold Cyprus. WAKE T9. T9 PLAN: Qadesh (Babylonia, bought walls, yield 30): mover from byblos with supporter at amurru (2 v walls 1). Babylonia's mari army may support the walls (then 2 v 2 bounces, nothing lost; retry or give up). Staging provinces next to qadesh that I can use are only byblos and amurru (damascus and tyre are bought walls, cannot hold my troops), so a 3rd attacker needs Ugarit or Carchemish first. Frontage insight: Babylonia can reach my north only through mari -> damascus (1 v walls 1 bounces), so war with Babylonia is low risk for me; war with Hatti is riskier (Ugarit and Carchemish border Amurru). c16 reaches Hatti T9 with my offer (Egypt keeps Byblos, Amurru, Cyprus, south; Hatti keeps Ugarit); reply back about T11. Do not hit Ugarit until I read Hatti's answer. c1 (Assyria) and c2 (Hatti) home T9: read their tablets. Gold is strength: spend only on units that conquer. Consider disbanding one fleet if nothing needs it (35 a turn). Do not trust anyone.",
  "summary": "Egypt (Napkhururiya, capital akhetaten). Goal: highest growth ratio (strength = 10 x yield + gold - back pay). T8 strength 4267 (2.08 vs start 2500), yield 395, net income about +165 a turn after upkeep 230 (3 armies, 4 fleets). History: T1 bought Tyre; T2 took Gaza; T3 took Megiddo and Tamassos, bought Damascus; T4 took Enkomi; T5-6 fleets north; T7 took Byblos (army convoyed from gaza, fleet support). T8: take Amurru (ends Alashiya). Holdings: akhetaten, byblos, damascus(w), delta, enkomi, gaza, megiddo, memphis, sinai, tamassos, thebes, tyre(w). Tablets sealed: k14 Babylonia peace (T3), k26 Hatti (T3: no troops against each other; Egypt holds Gaza Megiddo Tyre Byblos Damascus; Hatti Ugarit Carchemish Isuwa; Amurru and Qadesh need other's word; I am breaking the Amurru clause), k27 Mitanni (T3), k41 and k46 Arzawa (T5, T7: no troops or ships into any province of the other, Lukka included). Assyria: Pirissi pledged friendship T7, nothing sealed; c1 carries my tablet offer home (back T9). Refused Hatti's tablet barring me from Ugarit/Carchemish/Cilician Sea and Mitanni's reaches tablet. No gold sent to anyone. Rules learned: bought walled cities cannot hold my troops, conquered ones lose walls; walls hold 1; ties bounce; fleet at sea convoys coast to coast; fleets can support armies into coast provinces; empty provinces fall to any adjacent mover; support needs the supporter to be able to move into the target. Babylonia is main rival (1.64): holds Qadesh (walls), Mari (army), Ekallatum, Susa. Its only road to my north is mari -> damascus. Plan: Qadesh T9, then Mari from Qadesh; Ugarit/Carchemish only after Hatti's answer (c16 back ~T11). People: c1 (Assyria, back T9), c2 (Hatti, back T9), c16 (to Hatti, back T11). Do not trust anyone.",
