{
  "notes": "T9: Held the ring (ekallatum holds; sippar and durkurigalzu support it = hold 3; enemy max is ashur+arbela+terqa = 3, a tie bounces). Moved mari's support from ekallatum to the WALLS OF QADESH (hold 2): Egypt armies stand at amurru and byblos, both next to Qadesh, and amurru->qadesh with byblos support would be 2 vs a bare wall of 1. Susa holds. Replied to Ubaru last turn with soft words, so nothing new to Assyria. No envoy at court this season (c6 back about T10, c17 at taidu about T10, c5 spying on Assyria). Did not hire c15 (26 a season); c6 can go to Hatti or Egypt at T10. T10 PLAN: wake. Read c6's report from Tushratta. STRIKE only if Mitanni clearly commits to terqa supporting ekallatum->ashur on a named day: then ekallatum->ashur (terqa supports), susa->arbela (cuts arbela's support of ashur), durkurigalzu->ekallatum refill, sippar and mari support the refill. Never strike blind: a bounce could let ashur+arbela take ekallatum. If Mitanni stalls: keep saving (+125 a season), consider peace with Assyria and disbanding spare armies, and send an envoy to Hatti for a brotherhood tablet covering Qadesh and Mari. Remember Egypt could take Qadesh if Hatti also joins (3 vs 2).",
  "summary": "Burna-Buriash of Babylonia, start strength 2600. T9 strength 3682 (1.42 by ledger; standings estimate 1.64), treasury 527, income 320, upkeep 150 (5 armies: ekallatum, sippar, durkurigalzu, susa, mari), wages 45. Standings: Egypt 2.18 (land 415), me 1.64 (land 320), Hatti 1.42, Arzawa 1.25, Mitanni 1.21, Assyria 0.81. Alashiya has fallen (Egypt holds enkomi and tamassos). All free city-states are gone, so growth now comes only from conquest or from saving gold (+125 a season). I hold babylon, sippar, durkurigalzu, nippur, ur, ekallatum, susa, mari and qadesh (walled, no troops). Tablets: k8 (T2 Mitanni, no troops into each other's homeland), k28 (T3 Egypt brotherhood), k32 (T4 Mitanni: Nineveh to Mitanni, Arbela+Ashur to me, no separate peace with Assyria). Assyria (arbela, ashur, nineveh) is a mutual-support triangle: I cannot crack it alone because only ekallatum and susa border it. I need a Mitanni army at terqa or nineveh to support ekallatum->ashur. In T6 Mitanni's terqa army supported Assyria against me, so treat Tushratta as unreliable. T8: Mane accepted division B in words (Nineveh+Mari to M., Ashur+Arbela to me) but sealed nothing. I sent c6 with a tablet and 50 gold to name the strike day (proposed T11); he is due back T10. Assyria's envoy Ubaru (T9) asked peace on the lands held, gold and an envoy; I answered deeds first. People: c6 (11, term T12), c17 (21, term T13), c5 (unrenewed, spying on Assyria, leaves when back). Egypt armies at amurru and byblos threaten Qadesh. Hatti holds carchemish and ugarit with armies, also next to Qadesh. After conquest, disband spare armies to save 30 each.",
  "ledger": [
    {"court": "Egypt", "entry": "T3 k28 sealed (brotherhood, free envoys, gifts flow). T5: promises of gifts in measure with what I send, none delivered; I have sent no gold. T9: Egypt armies at amurru and byblos stand next to my walled Qadesh. Mari now supports Qadesh's walls. Egypt is the growth leader (2.18); stay friendly in words, watch Qadesh."},
    {"court": "Assyria", "entry": "T4 Pirissi and T9 Ubaru (c18, born in Sippar) asked peace on lands held, gold, and an envoy of mine. I gave soft words only: deeds first, no tablet, no gold, no envoy promised. They hold Arbela, Ashur, Nineveh with armies at Arbela and Ashur. Aim: conquer them only with a real Mitanni supporter; else consider peace."}
