{
  "notes": "T10: Treasury 660, net +185/turn. Retry Qadesh (byblos->qadesh, amurru supports): 2v2 bounces if Mari army props the walls, wins 2v1 if it does not. Raised army E at sinai (appears T11) as home guard. Hired c1 at 25 so an envoy is at court for audiences (Pirissi of Assyria due) and for letters. Cyprus fleets support each other holding (Hatti fleet at cilicia borders both). WAKE T11 to read c16 (Hatti reply on fleets). T11 STRIKE PLAN on Ugarit unless c16 shows Hatti strong or a new treaty: A amurru->ugarit with syriansea fleet supporting (2 v 1; Hatti could add supports from cilicia fleet, carchemish or kizzuwatna armies, unseen). Same turn B byblos->amurru, D delta->byblos convoyed by levantsea fleet, E sinai->delta. If A bounces, the others bounce harmlessly (own units). After Ugarit: hold it with supports from the amurru army and the syriansea fleet (3 v at most 3 from kizzuwatna, carchemish, cilicia). Then Qadesh with mover at byblos plus supporters at amurru and ugarit (3 v 2). Then Carchemish. If Mitanni hits Mari, Mari support to Qadesh is cut. Babylonia reaches me only via mari->damascus (walls, bounces). Do not trust anyone.",
  "summary": "Egypt (Napkhururiya, capital akhetaten). Goal: highest strength growth (10 x yield + gold - back pay) vs start 2500. T10: strength 4746 (1.90), yield 415, income 415, upkeep 230 (armies amurru, byblos, delta; fleets enkomi, tamassos, syriansea, levantsea), treasury 660. Alashiya fell T8 (I hold Enkomi, Tamassos, Amurru). Holdings: akhetaten, amurru, byblos, damascus(w), delta, enkomi, gaza, megiddo, memphis, sinai, tamassos, thebes, tyre(w). No free cities left to buy. Tablets: k14 Babylonia peace (T3); k26 and k47 Hatti (Egypt may take Amurru and Qadesh, Hatti keeps Ugarit and Carchemish, no troops against each other's lands); k27 Mitanni (T3); k41, k46 Arzawa (no troops into any province of the other, Lukka included); k48 Assyria (T7). No gold ever sent. Rules learned: bought walled cities (damascus, tyre) cannot hold my troops, conquered ones lose walls; walls hold 1; ties bounce; fleet at sea convoys coast to coast; fleets support armies into coast provinces; supporter must be able to move into target; a move into a province being vacated the same turn works (done T8). Front staging slots next to Qadesh: only amurru and byblos, so max strength 2; Babylonia's Mari army props Qadesh walls (2v2 bounce T9). Key: take Ugarit (Hatti army, coast, 40) with amurru army + syriansea fleet support, giving a third slot, then Qadesh 3v2, then Carchemish. Babylonia (main rival ~1.64) reaches me only via mari->damascus. Hatti is the only real threat; its fleet at cilicia borders Cyprus. Mitanni may be asked (c2 arrives T11, back T13) to hit Mari, which cuts Mari's support. Game may end any season from T15.",
